// die_with_parent covers the child until it ends: a grandchild it started, still running
// when the child is waited for, outlives this program too, which ends normally, unless
// wait ends it (group with leftovers = kill, Proc/leftovers). On Windows wait clears the
// Job Object's KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE before it closes it; on Linux PR_SET_PDEATHSIG was only
// ever the child's.
// The child is tests/helpers/child.ctx, as `start_beat PATH go`: it starts a grandchild that
// makes the file PATH grow for a minute, prints `started` and ends. That the grandchild still
// runs is the file growing in the second after (`beats PATH`), and that it has ended is the
// file no longer growing (`ends PATH`); `stop_beat` ends a grandchild that was left running.
//# build child: {home}/tests/helpers/child.ctx
//# build program: main.ctx

// the child without a group
//# make dir plain
//# $ {program} {child} plain plain/file
//# timeout: 30
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| started
//| 0
//# $ {child} beats plain/file
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| running
//# $ {child} stop_beat plain/file
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| stopped

// the child in a group of its own
//# make dir group
//# $ {program} {child} group group/file
//# timeout: 30
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| started
//| 0
//# $ {child} beats group/file
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| running
//# $ {child} stop_beat group/file
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| stopped
